    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class (the others are the abstract base and a helper), with both tests passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on owners.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `ownerSegment` property to the `OwnerDto` schema as a string enum with the four allowed values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`). The OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum` from this.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `@Mapping` binding and an `ownerSegment(Owner)` default method that:\n   - Picks `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - Picks `METRO` when `locality(owner)` is a known region (`NSW`/`VIC`/`QLD`), else `REGIONAL`.\n   - Combines them as `<TIER>_<AREA>` and returns the corresponding enum.\n\nThis reuses the existing `membershipLevel` and `locality` derivations, matching the surrounding mapper idioms. Both new acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass, and the full suite builds green.",
